            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nDefinition of highlight groups is a responsibility of a color scheme. In particular:\n- [This](https://github.com/ellisonleao/gruvbox.nvim/blob/15958f5ee43e144856cd2084ce6c571bfdb44504/lua/gruvbox.lua#L1087-L1092) is how relevant highlight groups are defined.\n- [This](https://github.com/ellisonleao/gruvbox.nvim/blob/15958f5ee43e144856cd2084ce6c571bfdb44504/lua/gruvbox.lua#L309-L310) is how `StatusLine` highlight group is defined, with which attributes are combined. As you can see, it has `reverse` set to [`true` by default](https://github.com/ellisonleao/gruvbox.nvim/blob/15958f5ee43e144856cd2084ce6c571bfdb44504/lua/gruvbox.lua#L63).\n\nThe solution here is either to set `reverse = false` in the config or update `MiniStatuslineModeXxx` highlight groups to also have `nocombine = true`.\n\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.statusline'.",
