            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Could you, for my understanding only, speak a little about why this didn't cause any issue in v0.10.4?\n\nBecause neovim/neovim#29976 is a change that is available in the Nightly releases and will be available in 0.11. Not all changes on Neovim's `master` branch go into patch releases (0.10.3, 0.10.4, and so on) even if they were done before the release. Mostly fixes to the functionality available in the stable release are put into patch releases.\n\n> And how should the colorscheme best be updated to fix this while also not causing any issues for those on older neovim versions, thanks.\n\nThat was already an answer:\n\n> The solution here is either to set `reverse = false` in the config or update `MiniStatuslineModeXxx` highlight groups to also have `nocombine = true`.\n\nIn particular, setting `nocombine = true` for all highlight groups which are used in statusline plugins (not only in 'mini.statusline') should avoid them being affected by the `reverse = true` in the `StatusLine` group.",
